# Code Comparison: Before & After

## Error Handling

### ❌ BEFORE: No Error Handling
```javascript
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  res.json([
    { id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' },
    { id: 2, name: 'Bob', email: 'bob@example.com' },
  ]);
});
```

**Problems:**
- No try-catch blocks
- Any runtime error crashes the app
- No error middleware
- Unhandled rejections
- No error logging

---

### ✅ AFTER: Comprehensive Error Handling
```javascript
app.get('/users', sanitizeQuery, (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    let page = req.query.page ? parseInt(req.query.page, 10) : 1;
    let limit = req.query.limit ? parseInt(req.query.limit, 10) : 10;

    if (!Number.isInteger(page) || page < 1) {
      throw new APIError('Page must be a positive integer', 400);
    }
    if (!Number.isInteger(limit) || limit < 1 || limit > 100) {
      throw new APIError('Limit must be between 1 and 100', 400);
    }

    const allUsers = [...];
    const startIndex = (page - 1) * limit;
    const users = allUsers.slice(startIndex, startIndex + limit);

    if (users.length === 0) {
      throw new APIError('No users found', 404);
    }

    res.json({
      success: true,
      data: users,
      pagination: { page, limit, total: allUsers.length, pages: Math.ceil(allUsers.length / limit) }
    });
  } catch (error) {
    next(error); // Pass to error middleware
  }
});

// Global error handler
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  console.error({
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    method: req.method,
    url: req.originalUrl,
    error: err.message,
    stack: NODE_ENV === 'development' ? err.stack : undefined,
  });

  if (err instanceof APIError) {
    return res.status(err.statusCode).json({
      success: false,
      error: err.message,
    });
  }

  const statusCode = err.statusCode || 500;
  const message = NODE_ENV === 'production' ? 'Internal server error' : err.message;

  res.status(statusCode).json({
    success: false,
    error: message,
  });
});
```

**Improvements:**
- ✅ Try-catch blocks for all logic
- ✅ Custom APIError class
- ✅ Proper HTTP status codes
- ✅ Error logging with context
- ✅ Environment-aware error messages
- ✅ Centralized error handling

---

## Input Validation

### ❌ BEFORE: No Validation
```javascript
app.post('/users', (req, res) => {
  const { name, email } = req.body;

  const newUser = {
    id: Math.random(),
    name: name,           // No validation!
    email: email          // No validation!
  };

  res.json(newUser);
});
```

**Problems:**
- No type checking
- No length validation
- No email format validation
- No sanitization
- Vulnerable to injection attacks
- No error messages

---

### ✅ AFTER: Robust Validation
```javascript
app.post('/users', strictLimiter, (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    const { name, email } = req.body;

    // 1. Type validation
    if (!name || typeof name !== 'string') {
      throw new APIError('Name is required and must be a string', 400);
    }
    if (!email || !validator.isEmail(email)) {
      throw new APIError('Valid email is required', 400);
    }

    // 2. Sanitization
    const sanitizedName = validator.trim(validator.escape(name));
    const sanitizedEmail = validator.normalizeEmail(email);

    // 3. Length constraints
    if (sanitizedName.length < 2 || sanitizedName.length > 100) {
      throw new APIError('Name must be between 2 and 100 characters', 400);
    }

    // 4. Create with validated data
    const newUser = {
      id: Math.random(),
      name: sanitizedName,
      email: sanitizedEmail,
    };

    res.status(201).json({
      success: true,
      message: 'User created successfully',
      data: newUser,
    });
  } catch (error) {
    next(error);
  }
});
```

**Improvements:**
- ✅ Type checking
- ✅ Format validation (email)
- ✅ HTML escaping
- ✅ Whitespace trimming
- ✅ Email normalization
- ✅ Length constraints
- ✅ Clear error messages

